From 436ce80965e0c09bfb0d3b715b05647ea6920e56 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:07:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] coord-diag: one-job route-leak diagnosis for
 coordinate-fusion GT runs

scripts/submit/coord-diag.sh [RUN_NAME] [ITER] (ln01, 4 GPUs, sequential):
own eval coverage check (every val_unseen episode exactly once), then
training-free variants of one checkpoint on all GPUs: occupancy_only,
cross_scene donor, nomap, coordinate_fusion off, cell_shuffle and
mentioned_only, with a summary table and paired SR delta vs own.
Derived namespaces are built on the fly (skipped when present) and never
inside the partner checkout; finished evals are skipped on resubmit.

eval_run.sh: EXTRA_ARGS (appended after eval_args.txt, so it overrides)
and EVAL_SUFFIX (separate result directory, required with EXTRA_ARGS).
make_ablated_gt_cache.py: --mode cross_scene (GT analogue of the LLM
raster donor test, same donor rule; assignment written to CSV).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018KbMocArNDLzFB1JmiiY2U
